## scripts/fpga-flow-init :: the template's own instructions count as unfilled work
# `templates/design.mk.in:12` reads "#   1. Fill in every <<FILL IN>>. ..." - a
# literal marker inside the instructions. A project that has made every real
# decision still gets `MISS UNFILLED PLACEHOLDERS  1 marker(s) in 1 file(s)`
# pointing at a comment, and the only way to clear it is to delete the
# instructions telling you what to do. Nothing in the next-steps text says so.
# Expressed as t_known_defect init.complete.decisions, so it goes RED when fixed.
# FIX: in the TEMPLATE, not the checker - spell the instruction without a
# literal marker.

## scripts/fpga-flow-init :: an empty write refuses (exit 2) instead of failing (exit 1)
# `install_one` line 293: `[ -s "$dst" ] || refuse "wrote an empty $dst..."`.
# CONTRACT section 10 reserves exit 2 for "refused - nothing was written", and
# this path runs AFTER expand() created the file and after earlier templates are
# already installed. Measured: rc=2 with files already on disk. The script's own
# header says why it matters - "a caller that cannot tell those apart retries the
# wrong one".
# Expressed as t_known_defect init.exitcode.emptywrite, so it goes RED when fixed.
# FIX: `fail` (exit 1), not `refuse`.

